Requests again, for each new still image, the tiles and glyph ranges whose
load failed. A still image fails at the first resource error, and the engine
never requested a failed resource again on its own: a file source that doesn't
retry left a failed vector tile pending and a failed glyph range unparsed, so
the next still image on the map never finished, and one over a failed raster
tile finished without it
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/786).
Upstream: not proposed

